\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For each fixed $J>0$ and $U\leq J$ on $sinh(2J)=\exp (-2U)$, do the Ashkin–Teller current height, wired and free cluster collections, and distinguished boundary component converge jointly on every admissible Jordan-domain lattice approximation to the source-normalized GFF, its associated continuum cluster collections, and its specified symmetric two-valued set? Use $H^s_loc$ for every $s<-1$, cluster matching, and Hausdorff convergence for the distinguished component.

\subsection{Short English statement}
For each fixed $J>0$ and $U\leq J$ on $sinh(2J)=\exp (-2U)$, do the Ashkin–Teller current height, wired and free cluster collections, and distinguished boundary component converge jointly on every admissible Jordan-domain lattice approximation to the source-normalized GFF, its associated continuum cluster collections, and its specified symmetric two-valued set? Use $H^s_loc$ for every $s<-1$, cluster matching, and Hausdorff convergence for the distinguished component.

