\section*{The joint GFF and cluster limit of critical Ashkin–Teller currents}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents a proof in the selected manuscript. Along the critical Ashkin--Teller line, the height and both nested current-cluster systems are claimed to converge jointly to one Gaussian field and its canonical recursive two-valued local sets.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
Exact cuts and spatial comparisons establish reflection-positive covariance and Gaussian Laplace screening. Stopped local-set exploration keeps the current clusters coupled to the same field, and iteration retains every nesting level together with the wired boundary cluster, including the four-state endpoint.

\subsection{Scope relative to this problem}
Along the critical Ashkin--Teller line, the height and both nested current-cluster systems are claimed to converge jointly to one Gaussian field and its canonical recursive two-valued local sets. The question retains these same parameters and conventions. Within these assumptions, this is a claimed affirmative answer to the stated question.

\subsection{Formal verification}
